<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Valtierra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1110">1110</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Valtierra was fought on 24 January 1110 near Valtierra in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-al-mustain-ii">Ahmad al-Mustain II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a>, returning from a raid into Christian territory, was defeated and killed by the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-i-of-aragon">Alfonso I of Aragon</a>. His death left Zaragoza unable to resist, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> occupied the city later that year.</p></div>
